  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 1245 PM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nZonal flow aloft dominates the Long Term forecast period. This \nresults in steady/near-normal temperatures on Wednesday and \nThursday, with highs in the upper 60s to mid 70s for most. A cold \nfront arrives sometime on Thursday and again Saturday, yielding \nafternoon highs in the 60s areawide (low 60s for many possible on \nSaturday and Sunday). Though it should be noted there is some \nuncertainty in the timing of the fronts. At this time, the NBM shows \nlow to medium PoPs (10-40%) across the area Friday night into \nSaturday. However, this is probably overdone as the NBM likely has a \nwet bias due to recent rains. Additionally, the westerly flow aloft \nshould keep conditions mostly dry during this timeframe. Stay tuned \nas we will continue to monitor trends and adjust the forecast as \nneeded.\n\nGreening",
